==German==

===Etymology===
Teenage slang. More literally, "to get on someone's cookie". The original reference is uncertain, but is probably a playful substitution of ''Keks'' for several other words which produce the same result (see synonyms below). This is possibly related to other idioms such as {{m|de|einen weichen Keks haben}} and {{m|de|einen am Keks haben}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|[aʊ̯f deːn ˈkeːks ˌɡeːən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-auf den Keks gehen.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|auf_den_Keks_gehen<ging,gegangen.sein>}}

# {{lb|de|idiom}} to [[get on someone's nerves]]
#: {{syn|de|auf die Nerven gehen|auf den Geist gehen|auf den Zeiger gehen|auf den Senkel gehen|auf den Wecker gehen}}
#: {{ux|de|Du '''gehst''' mir voll '''auf den Keks'''!|You're really '''getting on my nerves'''!}}

